      <h2>Certification of trust in Connecticut</h2>
      <p>After the declaration is signed and the trust is funded, a certificate of trust is what institutions actually ask to see. Connecticut lists the required contents at Conn. Gen. Stat. § 45a-499a. The section-by-section detail sits on its own page.</p>
      <p>See the <a href="/certificate-of-trust/connecticut/">Certificate of Trust for Connecticut</a> for the complete state requirements, and the <a href="/guide/what-is-a-certificate-of-trust/">what is a certificate of trust</a> guide for how the document works.</p>
